WEBVTT

00:08.008 --> 00:10.385
HOME SWEET HOME

00:10.468 --> 00:12.345
I made this sushi.

00:12.429 --> 00:15.932
Never thought I'd get
a homemade dish from you, Mr. En!

00:16.016 --> 00:17.726
Now eat.

00:17.809 --> 00:19.352
Sushi with raw meat?

00:19.436 --> 00:21.980
You even cut the meat
into mushroom shapes.

00:22.063 --> 00:23.606
That's so you, En.

00:23.690 --> 00:25.608
Can I just eat the meat on top?

00:31.614 --> 00:33.241
It's really delicious!

00:33.324 --> 00:34.617
It's nice and fatty!

00:34.701 --> 00:36.119
Extra sauce, please!

00:38.580 --> 00:40.248
Where are we?

00:40.331 --> 00:43.001
- The sushi's gone!
- There's nothing here!

00:43.084 --> 00:48.506
Someone must've used magic
to make everything but us disappear.

00:49.466 --> 00:52.260
- Mr. Chota, long time no see.
- What?

00:54.387 --> 00:56.056
I'm back to normal!

00:56.139 --> 00:59.684
Relax, everyone.
This place exists in our dream.

00:59.768 --> 01:00.935
Mr. En!

01:01.019 --> 01:02.437
In our dream?

01:02.520 --> 01:07.567
Actually, that sushi topping was
a new kind of mushroom from my farm.

01:08.151 --> 01:10.570
Its name is Dream Machine.

01:10.653 --> 01:13.073
It wasn't meat? That's terrible!

01:13.656 --> 01:17.577
If you pull it apart, it looks like meat.
Even the taste's close.

01:18.787 --> 01:24.584
This mushroom puts you into a deep sleep
where you can shape any dream you want.

01:24.667 --> 01:28.421
If a few people eat it at once,
they can share the same dream.

01:28.505 --> 01:29.589
Meow.

01:29.672 --> 01:33.718
Next month, I plan to launch it
under my food brand.

01:33.802 --> 01:36.346
I had you all serve as test subjects.

01:36.846 --> 01:40.517
The dream I want... That means...

01:43.561 --> 01:46.523
This is awesome!
This Dream Machine's great!

01:47.107 --> 01:48.817
Aren't you too big?

01:49.901 --> 01:52.779
- Nikaido, why are you in Chota's form?
- What?

01:52.862 --> 01:57.450
Maybe it's because
I was thinking about Chota.

01:57.534 --> 02:02.580
He hasn't been around lately,
so I figured Mr. En was missing him.

02:02.664 --> 02:06.960
That's impossible.
Go back to normal. You're an eyesore.

02:08.962 --> 02:10.964
Hey, is this the Hole?

02:11.589 --> 02:14.217
- Same filthy town as always.
- Whatever.

02:16.928 --> 02:17.846
Dammit.

02:17.929 --> 02:21.099
There's that lizard bastard and Nikaido.

02:25.186 --> 02:26.813
Mr. En, step back!

02:38.324 --> 02:41.828
How's that, boss?
The Dream Machine's great!

02:43.872 --> 02:45.957
Ebisu, your dream is...

02:46.833 --> 02:48.334
No, never mind.

02:48.960 --> 02:53.715
As expected, it looks like it'll sell
to losers like Fujita who hate reality.

02:54.257 --> 02:56.467
Nikaido, what do you wish for?

02:57.802 --> 02:58.970
What's wrong?

02:59.053 --> 03:02.182
- I hate you, En!
- What are you so angry about?

03:02.265 --> 03:03.433
Hey, Nikaido!

03:03.516 --> 03:05.059
My shoulders are getting stiff.

03:05.560 --> 03:08.396
Fujita, you're an excellent subordinate.

03:08.479 --> 03:10.607
I'll give you all of my fortune.

03:10.690 --> 03:12.734
Mr. Fujita, I admire you.

03:24.454 --> 03:26.789
Is that me?

03:31.085 --> 03:32.253
Wait!

03:36.966 --> 03:38.760
This house...

03:45.308 --> 03:47.018
This mask...

03:47.769 --> 03:49.979
It's my mask.

04:01.366 --> 04:02.325
Ebisu.

04:04.410 --> 04:06.871
Is your magic study going well?

04:06.955 --> 04:09.374
I'm counting on you, Ebisu.

04:12.502 --> 04:14.671
Mom... Dad...

04:19.300 --> 04:21.386
Nice! Dream Machine!

04:21.469 --> 04:24.514
I'd eat it every night.
Perfect fuel for the next day!

04:24.597 --> 04:25.640
Meow!

04:25.723 --> 04:28.393
Make sure you clean up properly, Ebisu!

04:28.476 --> 04:30.395
Yes, Master.

04:30.478 --> 04:33.523
Boss. Dinner is served.

04:33.606 --> 04:35.149
Really?

04:40.863 --> 04:42.865
What the hell?

04:42.949 --> 04:44.993
Did you dump all the useless crap?

04:45.076 --> 04:47.537
Did you get rid of the worthless garbage?

04:47.620 --> 04:48.997
Yeah, Mr. En.

04:49.080 --> 04:51.082
Mr. En...

04:52.083 --> 04:53.751
Mr. En! Everyone!

04:53.835 --> 04:57.338
It's me, Fujita! Wait...

04:58.339 --> 04:59.257
Wait for me!

04:59.340 --> 05:00.758
Nikaido!

05:05.096 --> 05:06.681
A hair dryer?

05:09.142 --> 05:10.518
Stop it!

05:10.601 --> 05:13.896
Mushrooms are weak to dryness, you know!

05:16.399 --> 05:17.400
This...

05:18.026 --> 05:21.154
This is the very scene
I fear deep in my heart.

05:21.779 --> 05:23.114
A true nightmare.

05:23.614 --> 05:27.160
So the Dream Machine
has effects like this too.

05:29.245 --> 05:30.663
Meow.

05:30.747 --> 05:32.332
No...

05:33.166 --> 05:34.709
I'm shriveling.

05:39.255 --> 05:45.553
So the Dream Machine is a mushroom
that lets you see yourself in many ways.

05:46.054 --> 05:50.558
Now then, my test subjects.
Do you think this will actually sell?

05:50.641 --> 05:52.935
Well, who knows?

05:54.187 --> 05:56.939
Mom... Dad...

07:24.986 --> 07:26.904
THE BEGINNING

07:29.490 --> 07:30.992
Ouch...

07:31.075 --> 07:32.910
Come to think of it,

07:33.494 --> 07:38.416
that bastard Dokuga
could have killed me, but he didn't.

07:38.499 --> 07:43.921
I've finally figured out
who killed me and the reason why.

07:44.005 --> 07:46.048
The Cross-Eyes.

07:46.132 --> 07:49.635
Why did I even join
an organization like this?

07:51.095 --> 07:55.558
Ever since I was a kid,
I couldn't produce any magic smoke.

07:56.142 --> 07:59.687
But turns out, there are actually
quite a few people like me.

07:59.770 --> 08:02.732
Guys who can produce smoke,
but only a tiny bit.

08:02.815 --> 08:05.318
And guys with useless magic.

08:05.401 --> 08:07.820
A bunch of guys like that.

08:08.404 --> 08:10.072
They were Cross-Eyes.

08:10.656 --> 08:12.575
This damn elite bastard.

08:12.658 --> 08:16.496
Stuffing himself with gourmet meals
in a high-class restaurant.

08:17.163 --> 08:20.583
- Hey, Risu, give me a hand.
- Yeah.

08:20.666 --> 08:22.585
- One, two, three!
- One, two, three!

08:25.379 --> 08:27.089
All right. Off you go.

08:31.636 --> 08:35.848
Risu, do you know
where they're being taken?

08:35.932 --> 08:39.810
I know. The torsos go
to the research facility in Berith.

08:39.894 --> 08:42.188
And heads go to the boss, don't they?

08:42.271 --> 08:46.317
The boss uses
those elite Sorcerers' bodies

08:46.400 --> 08:49.278
to become the strongest Sorcerer there is.

08:49.362 --> 08:52.907
And he's trying to save us,
his own people.

08:52.990 --> 08:55.326
Look. This black powder.

08:55.409 --> 08:57.954
I got it as a reward for the job.

08:58.037 --> 08:59.914
Now, watch.

09:08.756 --> 09:11.634
The black powder was our hope.

09:11.717 --> 09:16.222
But even that black powder
didn't work on me.

09:16.889 --> 09:20.893
Risu, what are you spending your pay on?

09:20.977 --> 09:24.230
Actually, I'm thinking
about going to school.

09:24.313 --> 09:26.983
School? You serious?

09:28.401 --> 09:30.319
I was serious.

09:30.403 --> 09:34.198
If I study at school,
maybe even I can produce some smoke.

09:34.282 --> 09:36.325
Let me introduce a new student.

09:36.909 --> 09:40.705
- This is Risu, who joined the class today.
- Nice to meet you.

09:40.788 --> 09:42.248
Those marks on his eyes.

09:42.331 --> 09:45.084
- Yes, it's the Cross-Eyes.
- What's he scheming?

09:45.876 --> 09:47.628
Now then, I'll begin the lesson.

09:52.550 --> 09:53.509
I did it!

09:53.593 --> 09:56.012
You brat, what the hell's wrong with you?

09:56.596 --> 09:57.763
You're lacking spirit!

09:57.847 --> 10:01.100
Like this is really
gonna help me use magic.

10:01.183 --> 10:03.269
Maybe I just flushed my money away.

10:03.352 --> 10:05.771
Who told you to sit down?

10:05.855 --> 10:08.274
You damn fool!

10:08.357 --> 10:10.735
That jerk. Just because he's a teacher...

10:10.818 --> 10:13.237
Spirit! Spir--

10:13.821 --> 10:15.740
Aikawa.

10:15.823 --> 10:18.743
You're looking a bit tense, teacher.

10:18.826 --> 10:21.829
Should I share a bit of my lunch with you?

10:22.830 --> 10:25.833
Today's self-study! Self-study, I said!

10:27.835 --> 10:30.588
Thank you, Aikawa.

10:30.671 --> 10:32.590
Nah, it's fine.

10:33.215 --> 10:35.968
Just buy me lunch, and we'll call it even.

10:36.677 --> 10:39.221
That's so typical of you, Aikawa.

10:44.101 --> 10:47.229
So, Risu. Are you having fun at school?

10:47.313 --> 10:50.816
It's okay, I guess.
It's full of carefree guys.

10:51.817 --> 10:55.863
You don't get to use magic
just by studying.

10:56.989 --> 10:58.449
You know, Risu?

10:58.532 --> 11:01.952
The organization bought
this apartment building recently.

11:02.036 --> 11:04.080
I wonder who's gonna live here.

11:04.163 --> 11:07.458
Who knows? Maybe some of the executives?

11:08.459 --> 11:09.335
Well...

11:09.418 --> 11:11.837
As you can see, rare magic

11:11.921 --> 11:16.634
includes those that manipulate
restoration, life, time, and so on.

11:16.717 --> 11:17.593
Therefore...

11:17.677 --> 11:20.680
Hey. I haven't seen
Maruyama and Tachibana lately.

11:20.763 --> 11:22.306
They haven't been to school?

11:22.390 --> 11:24.517
Now that you mention it...

11:24.600 --> 11:27.103
I heard Shimamura from Class 3
vanished too.

11:27.186 --> 11:29.855
Sorry we're late.

11:30.690 --> 11:34.110
Hey! What happened to you guys?
Those faces!

11:35.403 --> 11:37.363
Just fell down a bit, that's all.

11:40.157 --> 11:41.992
Also, in extremely rare cases,

11:42.076 --> 11:44.745
Sorcerers can possess
the power of a curse.

11:44.829 --> 11:49.500
If there were someone with such power,
the Cross-Eyes wouldn't leave them alone.

11:50.084 --> 11:52.253
There you are. Risu!

11:52.336 --> 11:53.963
The teacher's calling you.

11:54.046 --> 11:55.756
What? Me?

11:57.258 --> 11:58.843
Excuse me.

11:59.343 --> 12:01.762
You're here, new student.

12:01.846 --> 12:03.931
Well then, come in.

12:05.891 --> 12:09.895
According to the documents,
you can't produce smoke at all.

12:09.979 --> 12:11.272
Is that true, Risu?

12:12.356 --> 12:13.941
- Yes
- I see.

12:14.024 --> 12:19.739
Even if you showed up every day,
who knows how long you'd take to graduate?

12:20.281 --> 12:21.449
It won't be easy.

12:22.032 --> 12:23.951
And now, here's the thing.

12:24.034 --> 12:29.206
You're gonna buy this Magic Bracelet
as your educational material.

12:29.790 --> 12:32.084
Pay 50,000 nicks.

12:32.168 --> 12:36.464
If you wear this, you'll be able
to produce smoke in no time.

12:37.047 --> 12:41.218
Jeez. Selling fakes,
even though you're a damn teacher?

12:41.302 --> 12:43.554
You bastard!
How dare you defy your teacher?

12:45.723 --> 12:47.141
Ouch!

12:47.224 --> 12:49.560
Threats won't work on me, you know.

12:49.643 --> 12:53.397
Bastard. I won't forgive you. Be gone!

12:54.398 --> 12:57.651
I heard that. I totally heard that.

12:57.735 --> 12:59.653
Aikawa, you damn brat!

12:59.737 --> 13:04.408
I knew you were the reason
everyone got injured and went missing.

13:06.619 --> 13:09.622
Aikawa, you've always been a nuisance.

13:10.706 --> 13:12.374
Vanish!

13:19.882 --> 13:21.091
What do we do with him?

13:21.759 --> 13:24.887
If he wakes up, we might get expelled.

13:24.970 --> 13:26.722
- We're fine.
- What?

13:26.806 --> 13:28.808
I've got a plan.

13:30.810 --> 13:33.729
- Okay, I'm counting on you.
- Yeah, see you around.

13:35.022 --> 13:37.149
Where's that truck going?

13:37.233 --> 13:39.735
You don't need to know.

13:40.319 --> 13:42.530
But hey, you really saved me there.

13:42.613 --> 13:45.157
That bastard was the principal's relative.

13:45.241 --> 13:49.745
If you hadn't shown open defiance,
I might've been unable to do anything.

13:50.329 --> 13:51.664
Thanks.

13:52.832 --> 13:54.750
I just have a short temper.

13:55.835 --> 13:57.753
I'm Aikawa. Nice to meet you.

13:59.630 --> 14:02.007
My name is Risu.

14:04.009 --> 14:07.721
Aikawa, where the hell have you gone?

14:08.597 --> 14:10.474
So you're awake, Risu.

14:10.558 --> 14:13.269
Yo. Dokuga, I've been wanting to see you.

14:13.352 --> 14:15.771
There's something I want to ask you.

14:15.855 --> 14:20.150
Would've been better
to kill this bastard, wouldn't it, Dokuga?

14:20.234 --> 14:22.778
He probably came to steal something.

14:22.862 --> 14:25.197
But there's nothing valuable here.

14:25.281 --> 14:29.910
Don't get the wrong idea, Saji.
It's not that Dokuga chose not to kill me.

14:30.536 --> 14:32.162
He couldn't kill me.

14:33.622 --> 14:35.040
Ain't that right?

14:35.124 --> 14:37.585
Mr. Dokuga.

14:39.086 --> 14:40.546
Here we go!

14:42.339 --> 14:45.050
We finally made it to Zagan City.

14:45.134 --> 14:47.511
It's already night!

14:49.763 --> 14:50.764
Caiman?

14:51.891 --> 14:53.058
Hey, Caiman!

14:57.897 --> 15:00.316
I remember this road.

15:08.908 --> 15:11.577
MEMORIES SPIN ROUND AND ROUND

15:13.746 --> 15:16.290
"Zagan Magic Training School."

15:18.500 --> 15:20.419
My head!

15:21.003 --> 15:22.922
- Caiman!
- Big Bro!

15:23.005 --> 15:25.841
Caiman! What's wrong? All of a sudden...

15:27.051 --> 15:29.762
Is this a school?

15:30.262 --> 15:32.056
It's an abandoned school.

15:32.139 --> 15:34.558
Big Bro, why are you in a place like this?

15:35.184 --> 15:37.686
I've got business here.

15:38.729 --> 15:42.191
- You two wait for me here.
- Big Bro?

15:43.108 --> 15:46.195
Caiman. Could it be his memories?

15:51.659 --> 15:56.372
I feel like I remember
the way this floor feels.

15:56.455 --> 15:59.959
My head! It hurts!

16:00.793 --> 16:03.712
What the hell is happening to me?

16:11.053 --> 16:12.471
Wait!

16:15.432 --> 16:17.559
What the hell was that?

16:22.189 --> 16:26.485
Was I a student here?

16:26.568 --> 16:29.113
Or a teacher? A janitor?

16:30.489 --> 16:35.202
No, that can't be. That would mean I'm...

16:36.328 --> 16:37.663
like...

16:40.124 --> 16:42.710
some kind of Sorcerer.

16:43.961 --> 16:46.380
NAKATA
KASHIWABARA

16:46.463 --> 16:49.925
This is the teachers' room.

17:00.310 --> 17:01.270
RISU

17:04.857 --> 17:06.525
Risu.

17:22.541 --> 17:24.960
I'm Aikawa. Nice to meet you.

17:25.044 --> 17:26.920
My name is...

18:16.303 --> 18:19.515
- Caiman! So this is where you were.
- What the hell...

18:21.016 --> 18:23.435
- Big Bro!
- Caiman!

18:23.519 --> 18:25.938
NURSE'S OFFICE

18:26.647 --> 18:29.900
Caiman, what in the world happened?

18:30.442 --> 18:35.405
Your facial scales got torn off roughly.
Who did this to you?

18:37.407 --> 18:40.369
Don't tell me you did it yourself.

18:40.911 --> 18:43.330
- Found it!
- What is it?

18:43.413 --> 18:45.165
Bandage masks.

18:45.791 --> 18:47.584
You put it on your head like this.

18:47.668 --> 18:51.547
Then press the medicine button
and pull out the black pin.

18:51.630 --> 18:53.590
Finally, pull the red pins.

18:53.674 --> 18:54.508
These?

19:00.556 --> 19:04.560
There, all done!
You can even talk and eat with this on.

19:04.643 --> 19:06.103
It's amazing.

19:06.186 --> 19:07.855
Poor Big Bro...

19:07.938 --> 19:10.983
He must've suddenly started
hating his weird face.

19:11.692 --> 19:12.776
- Natsuki.
- What?

19:12.860 --> 19:16.029
Can you go buy
something to drink for Caiman?

19:16.113 --> 19:19.700
Sure, but don't leave me behind, okay?

19:27.374 --> 19:29.334
Caiman. You...

19:29.835 --> 19:31.461
Your eye crosses are gone.

19:32.796 --> 19:35.841
You remembered something, didn't you?

19:37.551 --> 19:40.345
Caiman, could it be

19:41.305 --> 19:43.223
you're a Sorcerer too?

19:46.059 --> 19:49.605
I used to go to this school.

19:49.688 --> 19:52.608
And I was here with Risu.

19:52.691 --> 19:54.610
But...

19:55.694 --> 19:56.820
Caiman!

19:57.487 --> 20:00.073
Who the hell am I?

20:00.157 --> 20:04.286
I feel something
really terrifying inside me.

20:04.870 --> 20:09.791
Nikaido, I might even end up hurting you.

20:09.875 --> 20:12.586
If that ever happened, I...

20:13.921 --> 20:14.796
Caiman...

20:16.215 --> 20:17.633
You'll be okay.

20:23.138 --> 20:26.058
HOME AGAIN

20:27.935 --> 20:30.729
- We're back!
- We're home.

20:31.647 --> 20:33.357
Little Bug, you're in the way!

20:34.149 --> 20:36.276
Thank you, Shin and Noi.

20:36.360 --> 20:41.531
Instead of thanking us,
tell us about the wax figure guy you saw.

20:41.615 --> 20:45.786
Got it. I'll go change, so just get
in the kotatsu and wait for me.

20:45.869 --> 20:47.663
Kotatsu?

20:50.415 --> 20:53.752
Shin, this furniture is interesting.

20:54.294 --> 20:56.171
Don't touch my leg.

20:56.255 --> 20:58.215
- Sorry for the wait.
- Don't touch me!

20:58.298 --> 20:59.675
TEST SUBJECT: AI COLEMAN

20:59.758 --> 21:02.928
Professor. That's your most important...

21:03.011 --> 21:06.682
Yeah. The starting point
of my research on Sorcerers.

21:06.765 --> 21:09.184
This is the file where I compiled it all.

21:09.268 --> 21:12.562
You're saying this is the wax figure guy?

21:12.646 --> 21:14.690
His face is totally unrecognizable.

21:14.773 --> 21:18.777
He was helping me with my research.

21:19.278 --> 21:22.698
Or rather, I began the research
at his request.

21:23.573 --> 21:26.201
Was the guy in this file a human?

21:26.285 --> 21:28.453
Yeah. I'm sure of it.

21:28.537 --> 21:32.249
The wax figure guy
and the man in this file...

21:32.332 --> 21:34.126
If they're the same person,

21:34.209 --> 21:37.462
then the Cross-Eyes' boss
is a human from the Hole.

21:37.546 --> 21:38.797
What?!

21:39.381 --> 21:42.467
Those Cross-Eyes guys can't use magic.

21:42.968 --> 21:44.636
It's possible, right?

21:44.720 --> 21:46.638
Mr. Kasukabe, where does he live?

21:47.222 --> 21:52.311
If I recall, he lived with his grandpa,
just the two of them.

21:53.979 --> 21:55.897
COLEMAN

21:57.190 --> 21:58.400
Maybe no one's home?

21:58.483 --> 22:00.777
- Noi.
- Roger that!

22:05.198 --> 22:07.451
Mr. Coleman?

22:08.368 --> 22:10.746
Looks like someone was here before us.

22:10.829 --> 22:13.790
Whatever. Let's look
for pictures of his grandson.

22:13.874 --> 22:15.959
Damn it! Who the hell did this?

22:16.043 --> 22:20.756
Shin! Should we bring this severed head
back to life with Kikurage's magic?

22:20.839 --> 22:22.382
Like we did with Risu.

22:22.466 --> 22:23.300
Ow!

22:23.383 --> 22:26.803
- That severed head...
- It just talked?

22:26.887 --> 22:29.306
Who are you calling
a severed head, you fool!

22:29.389 --> 22:32.309
I'm a bona fide victim of magic, you know!

22:32.392 --> 22:34.144
Look at this neck!

22:34.227 --> 22:36.438
They could've made my legs longer!

22:36.521 --> 22:38.065
Moronic Sorcerers!

22:38.148 --> 22:40.108
I thought you were dead.

22:40.192 --> 22:41.818
I was just taking a nap.

22:41.902 --> 22:43.111
Who are you guys?

22:43.195 --> 22:44.613
We're your grandson's...

22:44.696 --> 22:45.906
What'd you say?

22:45.989 --> 22:48.575
I can't hear you. I'm hard of hearing.

22:48.658 --> 22:50.577
I get it.

22:50.660 --> 22:53.580
You guys are here
to visit my grandson's grave.

22:54.623 --> 22:55.957
His grave?

22:56.833 --> 23:01.463
Ever since I ended up like this last year,
I haven't been able to visit the grave.

23:01.546 --> 23:04.049
You all coming really helped me out.

23:04.132 --> 23:06.218
It's already been 13 years.

23:06.802 --> 23:09.971
The kid was killed by Sorcerers.

23:10.931 --> 23:13.725
Now, go on and talk to my grandson.

23:13.809 --> 23:15.894
All right, let's dig him up.

23:15.977 --> 23:16.937
You bet!

23:17.020 --> 23:19.439
What?! What did you just say?!

23:19.523 --> 23:22.234
Hey! Cut it out already, you guys!

23:22.317 --> 23:25.862
You cursed wretches. Stop that!

23:25.946 --> 23:28.865
Knock it off! Hey! Can't you hear me?

23:29.449 --> 23:33.370
Thirteen years ago, I attended his funeral

23:33.453 --> 23:35.997
and saw his remains buried.

23:36.081 --> 23:37.958
If he really is in this grave...

23:40.544 --> 23:43.255
Here it is. The coffin.

23:43.338 --> 23:46.508
All right, then. I'm opening it up!

23:46.591 --> 23:47.801
Don't you kick it!

23:49.344 --> 23:50.720
- It's...
- The hell?

23:51.304 --> 23:53.723
It's empty. Not a damn thing inside.

25:23.688 --> 25:24.898
THE END

25:24.981 --> 25:27.192
What we learned in Episode 3.

25:27.275 --> 25:29.152
Risu and Aikawa are old friends.

25:29.236 --> 25:30.904
Caiman's memories return.

25:30.987 --> 25:33.073
Kasukabe knows the Cross-Eyes' boss.

25:33.156 --> 25:37.202
What we'll learn in Episode 4
is still hidden in chaos.

25:37.285 --> 25:39.913
This is Dorohedoro!
